4318275,-0.001100649475120008,-3.576278118089249e-07,-7.867782187531702e-06,-3.3641607761383057,-3.0278701160568744e-05,-0.00012385078298393637,-0.536689281463623,-0.00044955636258237064,-3.576278118089249e-07,-0.002058888552710414,0.0,-0.0003667397249955684,0.0,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-0.005094166845083237,-0.01948373205959797,-0.05347461253404617,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-3.6954811548639555e-06,-3.099436753473128e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,10061,400,64,4779,400,65,4779,400,66,4779,400,67,4779,323,400,68,3,387,279,12460,19703,315,279,23606,400,87,61,20,488,220,22,87,61,19,481,220,17,284,220,15,2418,220,7379,198,59,7265,90,6612,9,532,5,59,37018,90,64,61,19,15170,7,64,481,293,2376,64,481,272,2376,64,481,294,2376,64,481,384,9139,488,1124,37018,90,65,61,19,15170,7,65,481,264,2376,65,481,272,2376,65,481,294,2376,65,481,384,9139,90155,5,59,31610,488,1124,37018,90,66,61,19,15170,7,66,481,264,2376,66,481,293,2376,66,481,294,2376,66,481,384,9139,488,1124,37018,90,67,61,19,15170,7,67,481,264,2376,67,481,293,2376,67,481,272,2376,67,481,384,9139,90155,5,59,31610,488,1124,37018,90,68,61,19,15170,7,68,481,264,2376,68,481,293,2376,68,481,272,2376,68,481,294,9139,624,59,408,90,6612,9,92,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nLet $a,$ $b,$ $c,$ $d,$ and $e$ be the distinct roots of the equation $x^5 + 7x^4 - 2 = 0.$  Find\n\\begin{align*}\n&\\frac{a^4}{(a - b)(a - c)(a - d)(a - e)} + \\frac{b^4}{(b - a)(b - c)(b - d)(b - e)} \\\\\n&\\quad + \\frac{c^4}{(c - a)(c - b)(c - d)(c - e)} + \\frac{d^4}{(d - a)(d - b)(d - c)(d - e)} \\\\\n&\\quad + \\frac{e^4}{(e - a)(e - b)(e - c)(e - d)}.\n\\end{align*}","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"175283ef9db316cebac0e7ac39fac6f9f931df72facfd7e88e41c3ee8220735e"},"seconds":102.7862696647644,"seed":952297229667835115,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the given problem, we start by considering the polynomial \\( P(x) = x^5 + 7x^4 - 2 \\), which has roots \\( a, b, c, d, e \\). We need to evaluate the expression:\n\\[\n\\frac{a^4}{(a - b)(a - c)(a - d)(a - e)} + \\frac{b^4}{(b - a)(b - c)(b - d)(b - e)} + \\frac{c^4}{(c - a)(c - b)(c - d)(c - e)} + \\frac{d^4}{(d - a)(d - b)(d - c)(d - e)} + \\frac{e^4}{(e - a)(e - b)(e - c)(e - d)}.\n\\]\n\nWe can use the concept of Lagrange interpolation to solve this problem. The Lagrange interpolation formula for a polynomial \\( P(x) \\) of degree \\( n \\) at points \\( x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n \\) is given by:\n\\[\nP(x) = \\sum_{i=1}^n P(x_i) \\ell_i(x),\n\\]\nwhere \\( \\ell_i(x) \\) are the Lagrange basis polynomials defined as:\n\\[\n\\ell_i(x) = \\prod_{\\substack{1 \\leq j \\leq n \\\\ j \\neq i}} \\frac{x - x_j}{x_i - x_j}.\n\\]\n\nIn our case, we are interested in the polynomial \\( P(x) = x^5 + 7x^4 - 2 \\) and its roots \\( a, b, c, d, e \\). The Lagrange basis polynomials for these roots are:\n\\[\n\\ell_a(x) = \\frac{(x - b)(x - c)(x - d)(x - e)}{(a - b)(a - c)(a - d)(a - e)},\n\\]\n\\[\n\\ell_b(x) = \\frac{(x - a)(x - c)(x - d)(x - e)}{(b - a)(b - c)(b - d)(b - e)},\n\\]\n\\[\n\\ell_c(x) = \\frac{(x - a)(x - b)(x - d)(x - e)}{(c - a)(c - b)(c - d)(c - e)},\n\\]\n\\[\n\\ell_d(x) = \\frac{(x - a)(x - b)(x - c)(x - e)}{(d - a)(d - b)(d - c)(d - e)},\n\\]\n\\[\n\\ell_e(x) = \\frac{(x - a)(x - b)(x - c)(x - d)}{(e - a)(e - b)(e - c)(e - d)}.\n\\]\n\nThe Lagrange interpolation formula for \\( x^4 \\) is:\n\\[\nx^4 = \\sum_{i \\in \\{a, b, c, d, e\\}} x_i^4 \\ell_i(x).\n\\]\n\nEvaluating at \\( x = 0 \\), we get:\n\\[\n0^4 = \\sum_{i \\in \\{a, b, c, d, e\\}} i^4 \\ell_i(0).\n\\]\n\nThus, we need to find \\( \\ell_i(0) \\) for each \\( i \\):\n\\[\n\\ell_a(0) = \\frac{(0 - b)(0 - c)(0 - d)(0 - e)}{(a - b)(a - c)(a - d)(a - e)} = \\frac{(-1)^4 b c d e}{(a - b)(a - c)(a - d)(a - e)} = \\frac{b c d e}{(a - b)(a - c)(a - d)(a - e)},\n\\]\n\\[\n\\ell_b(0) = \\frac{(0 - a)(0 - c)(0 - d)(0 - e)}{(b - a)(b - c)(b - d)(b - e)} = \\frac{(-1)^4 a c d e}{(b - a)(b - c)(b - d)(b - e)} = \\frac{a c d e}{(b - a)(b - c)(b - d)(b - e)},\n\\]\n\\[\n\\ell_c(0) = \\frac{(0 - a)(0 - b)(0 - d)(0 - e)}{(c - a)(c - b)(c - d)(c - e)} = \\frac{(-1)^4 a b d e}{(c - a)(c - b)(c - d)(c - e)} = \\frac{a b d e}{(c - a)(c - b)(c - d)(c - e)},\n\\]\n\\[\n\\ell_d(0) = \\frac{(0 - a)(0 - b)(0 - c)(0 - e)}{(d - a)(d - b)(d - c)(d - e)} = \\frac{(-1)^4 a b c e}{(d - a)(d - b)(d - c)(d - e)} = \\frac{a b c e}{(d - a)(d - b)(d - c)(d - e)},\n\\]\n\\[\n\\ell_e(0) = \\frac{(0 - a)(0 - b)(0 - c)(0 - d)}{(e - a)(e - b)(e - c)(e - d)} = \\frac{(-1)^4 a b c d}{(e - a)(e - b)(e - c)(e - d)} = \\frac{a b c d}{(e - a)(e - b)(e - c)(e - d)}.\n\\]\n\nSubstituting these into the sum:\n\\[\n0 = a^4 \\frac{b c d e}{(a - b)(a - c)(a - d)(a - e)} + b^4 \\frac{a c d e}{(b - a)(b - c)(b - d)(b - e)} + c^4 \\frac{a b d e}{(c - a)(c - b)(c - d)(c - e)} + d^4 \\frac{a b c e}{(d - a)(d - b)(d - c)(d - e)} + e^4 \\frac{a b c d}{(e - a)(e - b)(e - c)(e - d)}.\n\\]\n\nDividing each term by \\( abcd \\):\n\\[\n0 = \\frac{a^4}{(a - b)(a - c)(a - d)(a - e)} + \\frac{b^4}{(b - a)(b - c)(b - d)(b - e)} + \\frac{c^4}{(c - a)(c - b)(c - d)(c - e)} + \\frac{d^4}{(d - a)(d - b)(d - c)(d - e)} + \\frac{e^4}{(e - a)(e - b)(e - c)(e - d)}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{0}.\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{0}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
